<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat drifts, some put option interest.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat drifts, some put option interest.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>January put options provided the main focus in quiet wheat futures trading on the Sydney Futures Exchange on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Fourteen A$150 January 1997 puts traded at a A$5.50 premium while the rest of the market continued to languish.</p>
<p>The only futures contract to change hands was January 1997, which rose by A$1.50 to A$158.00 a tonne in four trades.</p>
<p>Matt Kirk of McIntosh Futures Ltd said very thin trading on the SFE reflected a directionless Chicago. The put trades indicated that some producers remained interested in hedging.</p>
